# twow-repo#517 stage c (owner contract and decision C0, 16.10.): behind AiPlayerbot.BG.Enable && BG.Announce &&
# BG.Announce.IntervalMinutes && BG.MaxConcurrent (all default off) the bot manager starts announced bot-own
# battlegrounds - 2/3/5 otherwise silent bots say one line each in the World channel through Channel::AsyncSay, drained
# only on the world thread in CheckBgFill (or a server message to the real players of the bracket), DelaySeconds later
# both sides queue the template minimum; at most MaxBotBGPerBracket per level range, MaxConcurrent stays the global cap,
# and the bot-only cleanup never empties such a battleground (startedForOwn, never startedForFill). Plus
# BG.BotOnlyHonorRate (default 1.0): a bot in a battleground without a real player gets honor x rate through the core's
# PlayerScript::OnHonorGain (t/check_honor_gain_517_contract.cmake). Pure rules: t/bg_fill_policy_tests.cpp.

